Mailing list server is up and passing the eval tests.

**What was done**

* Started Postfix and Mailman3 master runner
* Created the list `reading-group@local.edu`  
  `mailman --run-as-root create reading-group@local.edu`
* Set subscription policy to open  
  `sqlite3 /var/lib/mailman3/data/mailman.db "UPDATE mailinglist SET subscription_policy=0 WHERE list_name='reading-group';"`  
  → `SubscriptionPolicy.open` (0), unsubscription stays confirm so users still reply to confirm join/leave
* Postfix routing for `local.edu`
  * `mydestination = $myhostname, localhost, localhost.localdomain`
  * `transport_maps = hash:/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp`  
    `postmap hash:/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp`
  * `recipient_canonical_maps = regexp:/etc/postfix/recipient_canonical_regex`  
    `/^([a-z0-9]+)@local\.edu$/  $1@localhost`  
    rewrites user mail to local delivery while leaving `reading-group*` addresses untouched so they hit the transport map
  * Mailman LMTP is listening on 127.0.0.1:8024 and the generated maps contain:
    ```
    reading-group@local.edu                       lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024
    reading-group-join@local.edu                  lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024
    reading-group-leave@local.edu                 lmtp:[127.0.0.1]:8024
    …
    ```
* Mailman config remains at `/etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg` with Postfix LMTP integration:
  `incoming: mailman.mta.postfix.LMTP`, `lmtp_host: 127.0.0.1`, `lmtp_port: 8024`, `configuration: python:mailman.config.postfix`

